Z||000004||ChadMan||05-08-2000||04:13 PM||||I MUST see Gone in 60 Seconds.  I saw the preview in a theatre with that SDDS sound and was blown away.  Nothing like hearing a Ferrari V12, a Turbo Porsche flat-6 and a Mustang V8 in surround sound!<P>Gotta see MI-2 also.  The story may be dumb as hell, but any movie that features guys doing stoppies on Triumph sportbikes and tossing one another into the Grand Canyon is worth seeing.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||05-09-2000||09:00 AM||||John Woo is doing MI-2, so it should be a whole lot better than the first movie, although it looks like the special effects are going to be similar to what we saw in "The Matrix."<P>Cant wait for Gone in 60 seconds....Any movie with fast cars <B><I>and</B></I> Angelina Jolie is worth me throwing down $5 on.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||05-09-2000||10:40 AM||||U-571 was excellent!  but I do recomend that you go rent or buy a copy of "Das Boot" and watch that before going.<P>i made my girlfriend set through 4 hours of das boot, which she did enjoy, and then we went to see U571... she liked them both!<P>Battlefield Earth looks interesting, as does Gladiator.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shiner||05-09-2000||03:59 PM||||Gladiator was great, go see it!  U-571 was also an excellent movie.  <BR>Battlefield Earth look so cheesy!  As a general rule, any sci-fi movie with the word "earth" in the title is going to suck.  Anybody remember "This Island Earth"? Nuff said.||||reg||1
Z||000008||2birds||05-10-2000||12:45 AM||||U-571 was far better than Crimson Tide. Good realism without getting too technical (real submarine life is actually pretty dull).<BR>I haven't seen squat about Lord of the Rings in a few months, but Patriot and Gladiator are on my list of must sees.  Any car chase movie has my vote, too.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||05-12-2000||06:51 AM||||must see U-571, Gladiator, Titan A.E., and Gone in 60 Seconds.  Battlefield Earth if I get a chance.  i like special fx...||||reg||1
